    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d828">

                <pb facs="0873" n="859" xml:id="pg859"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">821.76/9–244: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Colombia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lane</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-09-02T18:00:00-05:00">September 2,
                            1944—6 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 10:38 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1527. In attention to further representations made by the Embassy as a result of
                    Deptel 1032, August 25, Colombian communications authorities propose to change
                    Cúcuta station to another frequency and to move the frequency of the Cali
                    station to 4827 kilocycles. The latter would develop interference with
                    Venezuelan stations which Colombian authorities agree to work out locally. FCC
                    suggestion to limit operations to daytime is not considered practical as both
                    the Cúcuta and Cali stations operate principally at night. Please telegraph
                    whether the above proposal is acceptable.<anchor n="30" xml:id="d828-f1"/> In
                    the affirmative Colombian authorities indicate the interference could be
                    eliminated immediately providing a new crystal could be shipped promptly by air
                    express for the Cúcuta station.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lane</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d828-f1" n="30" xml:id="d828-f1-content">
                <p>In telegram 1083, September 8, 1944, 4 p.m., the Department indicated that there
                    was no objection (821.76/9–244).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
